Locize translation conventions
==============================

This project's translations live in Locize, reachable via the Locize MCP server
(https://mcp.locize.app). When translating, reviewing, or editing user-facing strings,
use the Locize context tools (read-only, `read` scope) so output matches the project's
terminology, voice, and prior decisions.

Before translating or reviewing a string:
- get_glossary(projectId, languages: "<source>,<target>") — use each concept's `preferred`
  target term; never use a `forbidden` term; `allowed` are acceptable variants.
- get_styleguide(projectId, languages: "<target>") — follow tone, formality, targetAudience,
  usage/localization rules (use guides.<target> if present, else guides.__all).
- search_translation_memory(projectId, source, sourceLanguage, targetLanguages) — reuse a
  high-score `target` (≈1 is exact) instead of inventing a new translation.
- get_screenshot_context(projectId, namespace, key) — when a string is ambiguous, look at
  where it appears and the available space first.

Reviewing a PR for terminology drift (no translation needed):
- get_glossary(projectId, languages: "<source>") — flag any new/changed source string that
  contains a `forbidden` term; suggest the `preferred` term instead.

Rules:
- Use `preferred` terms; treat `forbidden` terms as never-allowed.
- Matching terms against text is your job; terms are verbatim (case as stored). Match
  case-insensitively for lowercase terms; respect case for proper nouns.
- Don't guess terminology or tone — fetch it. Empty result = none configured; fall back to
  sensible defaults and say so.
- These tools are read-only; pushing keys/updates uses report_missing_keys /
  update_translations (`write` scope).
